Specific judgments:

- Tightenings (a), (b), (c): acceptable for this guard. `.*`, `(Edit|Write|Bash)`, `*`, empty, and absent matcher can work in Claude Code, but they are not simple enumerations of the guarded verbs. For this security wiring, requiring explicit `Edit|Write|Bash` or comma/list equivalents is a reasonable contract, not a moved false-green.
- Hyphen exclusion is also acceptable here. Official docs say hyphen exact matching requires Claude Code v2.1.195+, and no built-in `Edit`/`Write`/`Bash` name needs it.
- Claim (d) is correct. Official docs state `Edit, Write` is equivalent to `Edit|Write` on supported Claude Code versions, so the old Python-regex oracle false-redded comma lists. Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks, “Matcher patterns”.
- I don’t see arm 73 going vacuous. `gw_case` asserts empty `GW_NOTSIMPLE`; `gw_reject` asserts both the specific rejected matcher and missing coverage, so reject-vs-missing cannot collapse silently.
- I found one executable `fullmatch` call, not two: [scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:1064). It matches the fixed local grammar, not the matcher as a runtime regex. The remaining `fullmatch` mentions are explanatory comments.

